{"rank": 374, "article": "2026 United States Senate elections", "revid": 1360880128, "parentid": 1360865278, "user": "Tonyorlandoshouse", "timestamp": "2026-06-24T05:51:27Z", "comment": "/* Colorado */ The primary does not even happen until next week", "tags": ["mw-manual-revert", "wikieditor"], "size": 232248}
{"rank": 374, "article": "2026 United States Senate elections", "revid": 1360865278, "parentid": 1360864348, "user": "Yoblyblob", "timestamp": "2026-06-24T02:57:31Z", "comment": "I do not understand this edit summary much at all, but seeing as it has been removed multiple times in the past it should be discussed before inclusion- not a discussion held to remove it. Edit summaries aren't for discussion and an organization that has not had it's notability proven (with a page) should be discussed", "tags": ["mw-undo", "mw-reverted", "wikieditor"], "size": 233031}
{"rank": 374, "article": "2026 United States Senate elections", "revid": 1360864348, "parentid": 1360851537, "user": "MAWJ The Awesome", "timestamp": "2026-06-24T02:48:08Z", "comment": "I brought back Votehub... again. After reading the methodology I realized the legacy model is what the organization says should be used for apples to apples comparisons. This is the second time Votehub has been taken down, and due to Wikipedia guidelines on good faith additions, the policy is required to discuss removal of this forecast on the talk page. However, one of the main problems was that we were using the \"complete model\" which isn't being used now, so I expect the issue to be resolved", "tags": ["mw-reverted", "wikieditor"], "size": 235143}
{"rank": 374, "article": "2026 United States Senate elections", "revid": 1360851537, "parentid": 1360812040, "user": "~2026-35373-38", "timestamp": "2026-06-24T01:00:22Z", "comment": "/* Colorado */ Adding Senate election box", "tags": ["mw-reverted", "wikieditor"], "size": 233031}
{"rank": 374, "article": "2026 United States Senate elections", "revid": 1360812040, "parentid": 1360778087, "user": "OutlawRun", "timestamp": "2026-06-23T19:27:40Z", "comment": "/* Predictions */ Weird extra row", "tags": ["visualeditor"], "size": 232248}
{"rank": 374, "article": "2026 United States Senate elections", "revid": 1360778087, "parentid": 1360750123, "user": "OutlawRun", "timestamp": "2026-06-23T14:59:18Z", "comment": "/* Predictions */ I don't think VoteHub is established enough to include in tables like these. The \"complete\" forecast also includes prediction market odds, which I don't think we should allow, and unspecified \"expert\" predictions. Unclear if these are their own \"experts\" or just averaging other forecasters' ratings (like 270toWin does)", "tags": ["visualeditor"], "size": 232269}
{"rank": 374, "article": "2026 United States Senate elections", "revid": 1360750123, "parentid": 1360719574, "user": "Pikachubob3", "timestamp": "2026-06-23T10:25:07Z", "comment": "/* Potentially competitive seats */ Added in details about Iowa's race, and added that cooper appears to be the favourite (imo it is fair, most predictors have the seat him as lean D and his lead in the polls is quite strong)", "tags": ["wikieditor"], "size": 234267}
