{"rank": 374, "article": "2026 United States Senate elections", "revid": 1345927134, "parentid": 1345572201, "user": "~2026-17131-39", "timestamp": "2026-03-29T01:00:55Z", "comment": "/* Elections leading to the next Congress */ Removing Breslin. Candidates needed 30% to move on, she did not meet that threshold. https://www.coloradodems.org/press/colorado-democratic-party-concludes-2026-state-assembly-announces-results?fbclid=IwY2xjawQ1WJ9leHRuA2FlbQIxMQBicmlkETFGQmVobEtQV1Vubk5hT1M0c3J0YwZhcHBfaWQQMjIyMDM5MTc4ODIwMDg5MgABHq17U9MKJ8KzaqEtc_RpLGbfqCD74CWiN0D8uLv96FJS6y-4SGjmCPvQ-I4j_aem_tWJWw7WdgcoqyIBfcyphrw", "tags": ["wikieditor"], "size": 238926}
{"rank": 374, "article": "2026 United States Senate elections", "revid": 1345572201, "parentid": 1345433904, "user": "~2026-83524-3", "timestamp": "2026-03-26T21:01:04Z", "comment": "Alan Armstrong will be 64 at the end of its term.", "tags": ["mobile edit", "mobile web edit", "visualeditor", "mw-manual-revert"], "size": 239027}
{"rank": 374, "article": "2026 United States Senate elections", "revid": 1345433904, "parentid": 1345433706, "user": "TW929", "timestamp": "2026-03-26T02:06:07Z", "comment": "Undid revision [[Special:Diff/1345433706|1345433706]] by [[Special:Contributions/~2026-83524-3|~2026-83524-3]] ([[User talk:~2026-83524-3|talk]])armstrong is 62", "tags": ["mw-undo", "mw-reverted", "wikieditor"], "size": 239027}
{"rank": 374, "article": "2026 United States Senate elections", "revid": 1345433706, "parentid": 1345411407, "user": "~2026-83524-3", "timestamp": "2026-03-26T02:04:57Z", "comment": "", "tags": ["mobile edit", "mobile web edit", "visualeditor", "mw-reverted"], "size": 239027}
{"rank": 374, "article": "2026 United States Senate elections", "revid": 1345411407, "parentid": 1345342609, "user": "Kkuchnir", "timestamp": "2026-03-25T23:42:13Z", "comment": "/* Oklahoma */", "tags": ["wikieditor"], "size": 239027}
{"rank": 374, "article": "2026 United States Senate elections", "revid": 1345342609, "parentid": 1345342530, "user": "Thesavagenorwegian", "timestamp": "2026-03-25T16:26:36Z", "comment": "First off: It's Oklahoma Statues 51, §10, not the constitution. Second: it does not matter what Oklahoma law says, an appointee could turn around and run anyway. The eligibility for US Senate is set by the US Constitution, which is why people in prison can and do run for office. Third: I'm not entirely comfortable calling this situation \"term-limited\". Surely it's just a retirement? I suppose it's useful to call it that, to flag it as unique.", "tags": ["wikieditor"], "size": 239597}
{"rank": 374, "article": "2026 United States Senate elections", "revid": 1345342530, "parentid": 1345342069, "user": "Scoutguy138", "timestamp": "2026-03-25T16:25:52Z", "comment": "Reverted 1 edit by [[Special:Contributions/Patriots90|Patriots90]] ([[User talk:Patriots90|talk]]): They are simplifying wordy text and adhering to [[MOS:JOBTITLES]]", "tags": ["mw-undo", "twinkle"], "size": 238129}
